{
  "name": "02 AI lead scoring and routing",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI lead scoring and routing\n\n**Setup**\n1. Open the **Config** node: AI model, score thresholds (hot and warm), Google Sheet ID, Telegram chat ID.\n2. Describe your offer and your ideal customer in the system prompt (text in [square brackets]).\n3. Create a Header Auth credential for the webhook (for example header `X-Api-Key` with a long random value) and select the other credentials: OpenAI, Google Sheets, Telegram.\n4. In your Google Sheet create three tabs: **Hot leads**, **Nurture**, **Archive**, each with the header row from `sheets/scored-leads.csv`.\n5. Send leads to the production webhook URL with that header.\n\nThe tier comes from the numeric score and your thresholds, never from AI free text. If scoring fails the lead goes to the Nurture tab flagged as failed. The Slack node is disabled by default.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "2fc132e1-d2c1-4ef8-95e4-1658363c6f10",
      "name": "Setup notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -260
      ]
    },
